<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alcazaba of Málaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alcazaba of Málaga is a Moorish fortress-palace on a hill above the port of Málaga in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, built mainly in the 11th century and enlarged under the Nasrids. It stands above remains of the Phoenician and Roman town, beside a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, and is linked by walls to the higher castle of Gibralfaro. It is one of the best-preserved Muslim fortresses in Spain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alcazaba-of-malaga.jpg" alt="Alcazaba of Málaga" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alcazaba_de_M%C3%A1laga_overview.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
